<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aimery of Cyprus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1205</span> · Also known as Aimery of Lusignan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aimery of Lusignan was the first king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> and later also king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. He succeeded his brother Guy as ruler of Cyprus in 1194, obtained a royal crown from the Emperor Henry VI and was crowned king in 1197. In the same year he married Queen Isabella I of Jerusalem and became king of Jerusalem, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> until his death in 1205.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aimery-of-cyprus.jpg" alt="Aimery of Cyprus" width="320" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gustave Schlumberger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aimery_II_de_Lusignan.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
